// ⚠ THE EXPECTATION IN THIS FILE IS THE DEFECT, AND IT IS THE WORST REFUSAL IN
// THE MATRIX. A TUPLE-TYPED COLUMN COMPARED WITH `<` REACHES MLIR, WHERE THE
// QUERY COMPILER HAS EMITTED `arith.cmpi` ON A POINTER AND THE MODULE DOES NOT
// VERIFY.
//
// ⚠⚠ WHEN THIS IS FIXED THIS FILE GOES RED AND MUST BE REWRITTEN, NOT DELETED.
// Nothing unsound ships — the module is refused and no object is written — so
// the whole cost is the diagnostic, and the diagnostic is a type-system
// invariant violation reported by the compiler about ITSELF. No layer between
// the `where` clause and `arith.cmpi` asks whether the column has an order.
//
// THE MECHANISM. `el_ty_of_name` (stdlib/mem/wql/el.logos:174-181) launders any
// name the 21-row lattice does not admit to `EL_TY_INT`, so `(i64, str)` is
// spelled INT by the time the relational operator is emitted, and INT's own `<`
// is an integer compare. The value at that point is a pointer. This is the same
// laundering as `wql_domain_layer_blob_struct_col_fail`; the difference is only
// how far the wrong spelling travels before something notices — one clause
// later, and nothing does.
//
// ⚠ THE GENERAL FORM, AND WHY THE LATTICE'S DEFAULT-DENY NEVER REACHES IT.
// `EL_ORD_NO_CMP` exists as a row in the lattice for `String`, whose `<` the
// backend does not emit. But `String` is only ONE named member of an UNBOUNDED
// class — every type whose `<` mlir-gen does not lower — and the INT laundering
// happens one step EARLIER than the row is consulted. So a table with one row
// stands for a class with no bound, and this file is a witness from outside the
// table's population.
//
// ⚠ THIS TEST HAS A SIDE EFFECT, AND IT IS THE COMPILER'S, NOT THE TEST'S. On
// module-verification failure mlir-gen writes `logos-mlir-verify-fail.mlir` into
// the working directory — ~21 000 lines here. It is overwritten, not appended,
// and its own banner says the cause is in the diagnostics rather than in the
// dump. This is the first fail fixture in the corpus to pin an MLIR verification
// failure; if that dump ever becomes a problem, the fix is in mlir-gen, and
// silencing this test would only hide the defect it exists to record.
//
// WHAT IS ASSERTED is the MLIR verifier's own words. They name the layer with no
// ambiguity at all — no front end and no metaprog blob mentions `arith.cmpi` —
// so unlike its blob siblings this cell needs no argument about how the layer is
// identified.
package test;

use logos.std.wql.wql;
use logos.mem.collections.vec;

struct S { pub x: (i64, str), pub id: i64 }

pub deem q(ss: &[S]) { from ss s where s.x < (2i64, "b") select s.id }

fn main() -> i32 { return 0i32; }
